{"name":"Garden Weed","hex":"#786e38","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"},{"term":"weed","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant unwanted at the place where and at the time when it is growing.","Ellipsis of duckweed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove unwanted vegetation from a cultivated area (especially grass).","To pilfer the best items from a collection."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/weed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"},{"title":"Weed","blocks":[{"text":"A weed is a plant considered undesirable in a particular situation, growing where it conflicts with human preferences, needs, or goals. Plants with characteristics that make them hazardous, aesthetically unappealing, difficult to control in managed environments, or otherwise unwanted in farm land, orchards, gardens, lawns, parks, recreational spaces, residential and industrial areas, may all be considered weeds. The concept of weeds is particularly significant in agriculture, where the presence of weeds in fields used to grow crops may cause major losses in yields. Invasive species, plants introduced to an environment where their presence negatively impacts the overall functioning and biodiversity of the ecosystem, may also sometimes be considered weeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Stairs_with_weed.jpg/330px-Stairs_with_weed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weed","wikidata":"Q101879"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/500px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/1280px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/500px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The New Jersey Botanical Garden at Skylands Estate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkylands3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG/500px-%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG/500px-%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Partial view from the Botanical Garden of Curitiba (Southern Brazil): parterres, flowers, fountains, sculptures, greenhouses and tracks composes 